.TH ac "" "Administration"
.SH NAME
ac \- summarize login accounting information
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBac [\fIoptions\fB] [\fIuser ...\fB]\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.HS
ac -- summarize login accounting information
Usage:	ac [ options ] [ user  ... ]
Options:
	-d	Itemize for each midnight-midnight period
	-p	Itemize by individual users
	-w wtmp	Obtain raw statistics from 'wtmp' rather than '/usr/adm/wtmp'
If users are specified, only they are considered.
.HE
.B ac
summarizes the login-accounting data recorded in
.BR /usr/adm/wtmp .
That file, if it exists, receives a raw accounting record for each
login, logout, date change, and system reboot; by default
.B ac
prints the total connect time it finds there.
If one or more
.I user
arguments are given,
.B ac
prints a summary only of those users' connect time.
.PP
.B ac
recognizes the following options:
.IP \fB\-d\fR
Itemize the output into daily (midnight-to-midnight) periods.
.IP \fB\-p\fR
Print a separate total for every user.
.IP \fB\-w\ \fIwtmp\fR
Read accounting data from
.I wtmp
instead of
.BR /usr/adm/wtmp .
.SH FILES
.DS
.ta 1.5i
	\fB/usr/adm/wtmp\fR	raw login-accounting records
.DE
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.B accton
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
.B ac
complains if it cannot open the accounting file, and warns of a
possible bad file format if it finds an implausible record.
.SH NOTES
.B /usr/adm/wtmp
can grow very large; truncate it periodically.
